1
00:00:00,384 --> 00:00:02,144
(Wil:)I'm really happy to do this for you...

2
00:00:02,319 --> 00:00:05,759
(Wil:)...but not if she's gonna be a huge
pain in the ass the whole time.

3
00:00:06,323 --> 00:00:08,883
Are you gonna let him speak to me
like that?

4
00:00:09,059 --> 00:00:10,719
(Wil:)Well...

5
00:00:12,429 --> 00:00:15,419
(Sheldon:)...you're my girlfriend,
and I don't want you to be upset.

6
00:00:16,133 --> 00:00:19,533
(Sheldon:)Then again, Wil Wheaton's my friend,
and I don't want him to be upset.

7
00:00:19,703 --> 00:00:21,503
(Sheldon:)Hmm...

8
00:00:21,672 --> 00:00:23,042
(Sheldon:)This is a sticky wicket.

9
00:00:24,808 --> 00:00:26,138
(Sheldon:)What do you think?

10
00:00:27,144 --> 00:00:29,074
(Amy:)Can I speak to you for a second?

11
00:00:29,246 --> 00:00:31,006
(Sheldon:)I'll be right back.

12
00:00:31,181 --> 00:00:33,051
(Sheldon:)Feel free to play with yourself.

13
00:00:40,057 --> 00:00:43,027
(Amy:)I don't care for your friend,
and he's being rude to me.

14
00:00:43,193 --> 00:00:44,523
(Amy:)You need to ask him to leave.

15
00:00:44,695 --> 00:00:47,495
(Sheldon:)Amy, I can't just ask Wil Wheaton to leave.

16
00:00:47,664 --> 00:00:49,294
(Sheldon:)He's a minor celebrity.

17
00:00:50,567 --> 00:00:53,697
(Sheldon:)Once you explain who he is,
many people recognize him.

18
00:00:54,771 --> 00:00:56,141
(Amy:)Fine, then maybe I should go.

19
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:58,470
(Sheldon:)Could you? That would solve everything.

20
00:01:00,777 --> 00:01:04,217
(Sheldon:)You are the best.
I'll see you at dinner tonight?

21
00:01:04,381 --> 00:01:07,441
(Amy:)Sure you wouldn't rather have dinner
with your friend Wil Wheaton?

22
00:01:07,618 --> 00:01:09,708
(Sheldon:)Come to think of it, I would.

23
00:01:10,621 --> 00:01:15,021
(Sheldon:)You, little lady, are on fire.

